arged than the  leaders of china and russia meeting  during the games a desire to assert for  their own countries a place on the world  stage the fact is that sports  has been political from the beginning of  time and every olympics has had an  element of politics meantime eileen gu  has been denounced by some back in the  u.s everything about her is awful  goo could be beloved in either china or  the u.s but not it seems in both during  these politicized games eric sorensen  global news toronto  a former canadian women's soccer coach  has pleaded guilty to three counts of  sexual assault and one count of sexual  touching charges against bob berarda  were laid over a year ago for crimes  committed between 1988 and 2008. he was  the head coach of the vancouver  whitecaps women's team and the canadian  under 20 women's team both organizations  cut ties with him in 2008. more than a  dozen women have come forward with  allegations bharata acted  inappropriately  protests come with a cost ahead how the  disruptions are affecting businesses and  trade  you're watching global national  [Music]  there's some good news tonight for  potato farmers in pei the u.s has agreed  to resume shipments of island potatoes  to puerto rico that represents about a  quarter of pei's potato exports to the  u.s those experts have been on hold  since november when potato wart was  discovered in two pei fields the fungus  poses no threat to human health but can  reduce crop yields puerto rico does not  farm potatoes commercially so the risk  is low  well bands like that have a big economic  impact the ongoing so-called freedom  convoy protests are also having an  impact there are huge costs to the city  of ottawa for policing and lots of small  businesses already battered by the  pandemic have had to close tonight ann  gaviola takes a look at the economic  costs of these protests  it's really disheartening first bite  treats in ottawa's byward market started  the year off with a lockdown then the  protest convoy descended on nearby  parliament hill the financial toll is  significant as people and delivery  services shun the downtown core  it's in the thousands uh and it's  racking up doritos center ottawa's  largest mall with 175 shops has been  closed since the weekend affecting  thousands of employees and neighboring  businesses  mall owner cadillac fairview says the  continued closure of an important  community space loss of employment  income and the financial impact on  clients is heartbreaking given our  shared pain and sacrifice during the  pandemic  policing costs for the city of ottawa  are eight hundred thousand for policing  plus one million dollars in city  services every day the city is asking  for help from provincial and federal  governments including eighteen hundred  more officers which would bring daily  policing costs to two and a half million  dollars  for context security for a canada day  celebration runs north of six hundred  thousand dollars this eclipses that  uncertainty about how long this drags on  could mean long-term damage to tourism  hospitality and retail even if they  leave next week could they be back in a  month did they be back in two months  with cross-border traffic disrupted  analysts expect the price of goods  trucked in to go up the longer this  continues especially food and that's on  top of existing supply chain related  inflation the rcmp tell global news they  don't yet have a tally of policing costs  to taxpayers as multiple divisions are  involved but they'll have one soon the  mental cost that this can actually place  on people  is something we haven't thought about  but it's something that should be  considered this could be a major  disruption uh if the government can't  find a way to bring this back under  control and unite everybody politically  socially and economically the biggest  price to pay may not be easy to put into  dollars and cents  anne gaviola global news toronto  [Music]  let's talk about the oscars then next  can this year's nominees still spice up  the big screen  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  the stage is set for hollywood's biggest  night the 2022 oscar nominations are out  and once again the box office is no  longer playing a lead role half of the  movies nominated for best picture either  debuted or were quickly released on  streaming platforms mike derlay reports  on the evolution of the movie business  and the oscar  goes to  there was a time the oscars would  routinely draw over 40 million viewers  last year fewer than 10 million watched  a show that lacks songs spectacle and  star power are the oscars still even  relevant i think they think they are i  don't know if any awards  ceremony now that there are more than  four channels and that you can avoid the  oscars on the sunday night that they  happen if you want to i don't think any  award ceremony has that level of  importance  the last year was another tough one for  the movie industry memories of pack  theaters and blockbusters seem distant  you're the nominees for best picture of  the 10 movies nominated for best picture  most including west side story nightmare  alley and belfast have yet to make money  at the box office king richard and dune  from canadian double nominee denis  villeneuve were released in theaters and  streaming services at the same time the  others including the power of the dog  with its 12 nominations are streamers  the industry's in transition even if  movie lovers believe epics like dune are  meant for the big screen i don't think  theaters will ever go away i think  streaming has carved out a bigger space  than anyone would have expected in the  time allotted but that's mostly because  of the pandemic forcing everyone to stay  home watch movies at home and realize  you know if you have a pretty decent  setup it's cheaper it's more comfortable  and you can not leave your house i'd  like you to take me with you  whether it's a distant world or the old  west movies still captivate us  you are marvelous rose  and that golden oscar no matter how many  people watch  is still the ultimate prize for those  who set out to captivate  mike relay global news toronto  and that is global national for this  tuesday i'm donna friesen tonight's your  canada is kimberly british columbia  there are beautiful spots all over this  country please email us yours to viewers  at globalnational.com  thanks for watching hope to see you here  again tomorrow bye
 

